{"name":"Nova White","hex":"#f8eed9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nova","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any sudden brightening of a previously inconspicuous star.","Ellipsis of classical nova"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of novum"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nova"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nova","blocks":[{"text":"A nova is a transient astronomical event that causes the sudden appearance of a bright, apparently \"new\" star that slowly fades over weeks or months. All observed novae involve white dwarfs in close binary systems, but causes of the dramatic appearance of a nova vary, depending on the circumstances of the two progenitor stars. The main sub-classes of novae are classical novae, recurrent novae (RNe), and dwarf novae. They are all considered to be cataclysmic variable stars."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/Making_a_Nova.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nova","wikidata":"Q6458"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Nova-Eridani-2009-LB4.jpg/500px-Nova-Eridani-2009-LB4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Nova-Eridani-2009-LB4.jpg/1280px-Nova-Eridani-2009-LB4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Nova-Eridani-2009-LB4.jpg/500px-Nova-Eridani-2009-LB4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nova Eridani 2009 (apparent magnitude ~8.4)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANova-Eridani-2009-LB4.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/GKPersei-MiniSuperNova-20150316.jpg/500px-GKPersei-MiniSuperNova-20150316.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/GKPersei-MiniSuperNova-20150316.jpg/1280px-GKPersei-MiniSuperNova-20150316.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/GKPersei-MiniSuperNova-20150316.jpg/500px-GKPersei-MiniSuperNova-20150316.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"GK Persei: Nova of 1901","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGKPersei-MiniSuperNova-20150316.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Nova_in_M31.jpg/330px-Nova_in_M31.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/